      "name": "two-phase-move",
      "title": "Two-phase move",
      "description": "Move a path that other layers link to without making the order of their re-pins matter: the moving layer declares the move and keeps answering at the old path for a window, the dependent layers switch in any order, and the old path goes once nothing links to it. Use before moving or renaming a directory another layer links into.",
